About The Position

As a Data Scientist within the Pricing Analytics team at HP, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the future of how we set prices. Join our dynamic, highly skilled, and diverse global team, composed of economists, statisticians, computer scientists, natural scientists, and engineers, all committed to pushing the innovation frontier in pricing strategies for HP products. Your role will involve combining modelling skills, economic and business thinking, experimentation, and optimization methods to build intricate pricing algorithms for the most popular Printers and PCs in the market.

About You
• You have deep interest in customer and market behavior with a focus on methods to measure and anticipate it;
• You are passionate about uncovering answers to challenging questions using data and models;
• You feel accomplished when your pricing recommendations are implemented and you will go all the extra miles to make it happen;
• You are inherently curious, always eager... to learn something new on a daily basis and thrive in an environment surrounded by highly talented individuals.

What You Will Be Doing
• Develop and implement predictive models and algorithms to support pricing strategies;
• Collaborate with the business and product teams to understand market dynamics, competitive landscapes, and customer behaviours;
• Design and execute experiments to test hypotheses and validate pricing models;
• Build and maintain statistical models for forecasting and scenario analysis;
• Present findings and insights to both technical and non-technical stakeholders in a clear and compelling manner;
• Work closely with cross-functional teams to integrate data-driven insights into strategic decision-making processes;

What We Are Looking For (must-haves)
• At least 2 years of experience in data science;
• Master's degree or above in Computer Science, Economics, Engineering, or related disciplines;
• Proficiency in Python, R, and Spark;
• Strong coding and software development skills;
• Interest in pricing, economics, and consumer behavior;
• Experience in designing, deploying, and analyzing in-market experiments and/or AB tests;
• Ability to think creatively and invent original solutions to business and modelling challenges.

Bonus Points For
• Experience in deploying ML and data science solutions.
• Knowledge of price optimization approaches, B2B pricing, and a general understanding of main concepts from industrial organization literature.
• Basic understanding of finance and product economics.

About HP

Reinventing since 1939. We are one of the leading Print and Personal Systems technology companies in the world and our vision is to create technology that makes life better for everyone, everywhere. Joining HP is joining an adventure to reinvent the tech world and reinvent yourself every day

